-- title:
--   Lemma 6 — exponential weights for nonnegative estimates
-- statement:
--   Let $\eta>0$, let $\mathcal F$ be a finite set of experts, and let $\hat\ell_1,\dots,\hat\ell_T$ be nonnegative loss estimates, $\hat\ell_t(f)\ge0$. Let $u_t$ be the exponential-weights distribution
--   $$
--   u_t(f)=\frac{\exp(-\eta L_{t-1}(f))}{\sum_{f'}\exp(-\eta L_{t-1}(f'))},\qquad L_t(f)=L_{t-1}(f)+\hat\ell_t(f),\quad L_0=0 .
--   $$
--   Then for every expert $f^\star$,
--   $$
--   \sum_{t=1}^T\langle u_t,\hat\ell_t\rangle-\sum_{t=1}^T\hat\ell_t(f^\star)\le\frac{\log|\mathcal F|}{\eta}+\frac{\eta}{2}\sum_{t=1}^T\langle u_t,\hat\ell_t^2\rangle .
--   $$
--
--   Because the endpoint flow estimates are nonnegative pathwise, this second-order bound applies to them in Algorithm 2.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Experts are $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ and rounds are $0,\dots,T-1$; $u_t$ is the published `UnderstandingML.wmWeights`.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: $|\mathcal F|\ge2$ (standing, Sec. 2.1) → any $n$ (necessarily $n\ge1$, as $f^\star$ exists); reason: the bound holds for every nonempty expert class; specializes to $|\mathcal F|\ge2$
--   - encoding: rounds $t=1,\dots,T$ → $t\in\{0,\dots,T-1\}$; reason: Lean convention; same instances
-- source:
--   Zuo, Online Learning with Ordered Experts (via Two-point Feedback), STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 a6480b1e…fe429), Lemma 6, p.11; Appendix B.1, p.20

import Definitions.Def_UnderstandingML_Online
open Finset

namespace OrderedExperts

/-- **Lemma 6 (Exponential weights for nonnegative estimates).** Zuo, *Online Learning with Ordered Experts (via Two-point Feedback)*, STOC 2027 submission (held version), Lemma 6,
p.11: "Let `ut` be the exponential-weights distribution generated by nonnegative loss estimates
`ℓ̂t(f) ≥ 0`: `ut(f) = exp(−ηLt−1(f))/Σ_{f′} exp(−ηLt−1(f′))`, `Lt(f) = Lt−1(f) + ℓ̂t(f)`. Then for
every `f⋆`, `Σ_{t=1}^T ⟨ut, ℓ̂t⟩ − Σ_{t=1}^T ℓ̂t(f⋆) ≤ log|F|/η + (η/2) Σ_{t=1}^T ⟨ut, ℓ̂²t⟩`." The learning
rate is `η > 0` (Algorithm 2, p.11), and `L0 = 0`.

**Formalization Note.** Experts are `Fin n`; rounds are 0-based (`t ∈ range T`); `ut` is the published
`UnderstandingML.wmWeights η v t`, whose cumulative loss `Σ_{s<t} v s` builds in `L0 = 0`. -/
theorem lemma_6 {n : ℕ} (η : ℝ) (hη : 0 < η) (T : ℕ) (v : ℕ → Fin n → ℝ)
    (hv : ∀ t < T, ∀ i, 0 ≤ v t i) (fstar : Fin n) :
    ∑ t ∈ range T, ∑ i, UnderstandingML.wmWeights η v t i * v t i -
        ∑ t ∈ range T, v t fstar ≤
      Real.log n / η +
        η / 2 * ∑ t ∈ range T, ∑ i, UnderstandingML.wmWeights η v t i * v t i ^ 2 := by sorry

end OrderedExperts
